---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 26, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added a Switching Without Retyping section to every comparison and alternative page. It describes
    the four ways BreederHQ brings in what a breeder already keeps and links the
    <a href="/workflows/bring-what-you-have" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">Bring What You Already Have</a> hub.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>The 18 pages under <code>src/pages/compare/</code>: a new section before the closing call to action covering Scout record import, Fill &amp; Sign from your own PDF, importing an existing application form, and Application Links.</li>
      <li>The two Breeder Cloud Pro pages also describe the mileage import.</li>
      <li><code>compare/index.astro</code>: one line pointing to the hub.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Genetics wording</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The Good Dog, Breeder Cloud Pro, and best dog pages no longer list GenSol as a scanner-read lab or say Scout reads any lab.
      They now say Scout interprets results only for the labs and tests its catalog recognizes, and saves other labs' reports as printed.
    </p>
  </div>
